    "created_at": "2016-03-29T14:36:30Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-29T14:36:30Z",
    "body": "One thing worth considering in scheduling is that notifications become stale at some point.  For example,  a calendar app may want a notification to show only just before and during an important event.\n\nOne use case where this is important is when a laptop goes to sleep for a while, then the user opens up the laptop later.  Today, any notifications created just before sleep will be shown after sleep since AFAIK there are no signals about sleep/wakeup in the browser.  However with an expiration time no unnecessary notifications would be shown.\n\nI suppose this could be built into a richer alarms API, but that might still not cover sleep cases very well.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
